From: mscharged-port
Subject: Report draws that wait for a pipeline compile
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

A draw whose pipeline is not compiled yet waits for the compile: the frame
stutters. The demand statistics only counted these waits. The host can now set
a callback that receives each one after the compile, on the drawing thread:
the configuration's type, version, XXH3 key and raw bytes, the frame, the wait,
and whether the configuration was new on this computer (neither the bundled nor
the local cache had it) or known but not yet compiled for the render target
layout. The host logs new configurations so they can be added to the bundled
pipeline catalogue. Reports hold their own lock, never the pipeline lock, so
clearing the callback waits for a running report; shutdown clears it.

diff --git a/include/aurora/pipeline_cache.h b/include/aurora/pipeline_cache.h
index 1a399f6..d173f0f 100644
--- a/include/aurora/pipeline_cache.h
+++ b/include/aurora/pipeline_cache.h
@@ -91,6 +91,29 @@ bool aurora_end_pipeline_collection(bool submit);
  */
 AuroraPipelineWarmupStatus aurora_pipeline_warmup_status();
 
+/** A draw that waited for its pipeline to compile: one demand miss. */
+typedef struct {
+  uint32_t shaderType;    /* 0 clear, 1 GX: the pipeline_cache.db type */
+  uint32_t configVersion;
+  uint64_t configKey;     /* XXH3 key of the configuration (pipeline_cache.db hash) */
+  const void* config;     /* the raw configuration, valid during the call */
+  uint32_t configSize;
+  uint32_t frame;         /* frame of the draw */
+  uint64_t waitNanoseconds;
+  /** First use of this configuration on this computer: neither the bundled nor
+   * the local cache had it. Otherwise it was known, but not yet compiled for
+   * this render target layout. */
+  bool newConfiguration;
+} AuroraPipelineDemandMiss;
+typedef void (*AuroraPipelineDemandMissCallback)(const AuroraPipelineDemandMiss* miss, void* userData);
+/** Report every draw that waits for a pipeline compile, after the compile, on
+ * the drawing thread, with no pipeline lock held. Set after aurora_initialize;
+ * aurora_shutdown clears it. Returns once a running report has finished, so
+ * userData may be released after a NULL callback is set. The callback must not
+ * call this function.
+ */
+void aurora_set_pipeline_demand_miss_callback(AuroraPipelineDemandMissCallback callback, void* userData);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
